<reference id="_Toc235450348" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 1 — Paragraph in a concept topic</title>
   <shortdesc>Consider an HTML section titled "Product Parts Location" followed by two &lt;p&gt; elements describing the</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>concept</keyword>
        <keyword>parts</keyword>
        <keyword>printer</keyword>
        <keyword>Paragraph</keyword>
        <keyword>topic</keyword>
        <keyword>section</keyword>
        <indexterm>concept</indexterm>
        <indexterm>parts</indexterm>
        <indexterm>printer</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody>
      <section>
      <p>Consider an HTML section titled "Product Parts Location" followed by two <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> elements describing the product.</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Paragraph in a concept topic</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>HTML Input</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>
&lt;h2>Product parts location&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>Use this section to identify the parts on the printer.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>The printer has three main areas: front, inside, and back.&lt;/p></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>
&lt;concept id="product_parts_location">
  &lt;title>Product Parts Location&lt;/title>
  &lt;conbody>
    &lt;p>Use this section to identify the parts on the printer.&lt;/p>
    &lt;p>The printer has three main areas: front, inside, and back.&lt;/p>
  &lt;/conbody>
&lt;/concept></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
<p><b>Result:</b> Both <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> elements are mapped to <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> elements inside <codeph>&lt;conbody&gt;</codeph> in document order. The first <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> element is also extracted as <codeph>&lt;shortdesc&gt;</codeph>.</p>
         </section>
   </refbody>
</reference>
